{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/970445-what-breaks-if-you-return-to-ideas-from-the-earlier-draft","id":970445,"title":"What breaks if you return to ideas from the earlier draft?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T20:27:55-07:00","id":970445,"title":"What breaks if you return to ideas from the earlier draft?","content":"I've definitely come around to Beast after making a concentrated effort to actually read the book and learn to love the game, but two things have stuck with me out of the general muck surrounded the earlier Kickstarter/leak draft that I'd like to bring back, admittedly due to their similarities to Leviathan: the Begotten creating some Heroes and the idea of the Homecoming over the Devouring. While I know there's some thematic grumbling over both of these (the former is sometimes compared to victim-blaming, the latter creates some notions of dehumanization when bundles up in some of the misguided marginalization metaphor from the earlier draft), I feel like decoupled from their baggage there's still some neat value to be had there.<br /> <br /> Creating Heroes gives Beasts a nice external punishment that they're otherwise lacking without a 'Morality stat' like other games, that if you're careless in your feeding you risk creating a dangerous threat and turning a normal person into an obsessive Dream-compelled killer, and I think that's an interesting place to explore in the game. For the Begotten who follow the Lesson-teaching paradigm, creating Heroes on accident hammers home the monstrosity of what they're doing no matter what philosophy they comfort themselves with; I think that's rife with story potential.<br /> <br /> As for the Homecoming, I think it scratches a horror niche largely untapped in the CofD: the notion that you're not human and never have been. While many games follow a &quot;you're a human transformed&quot; and some have &quot;you've always been a monster,&quot; the only other game that at all deals with &quot;you've only <i>thought</i> you're human, but this is the real you&quot; is Werewolf, and that game (while awesome!) has many other themes and angles it works to address. I think the Homecoming is a much more evocative shock that the Devouring, which is somewhat vague in the text and risks feeling like a budget Embrace.<br /> <br /> So I'd love to hear from anyone else who's with me on this, or even from folks who want to talk me out of it. I think Beast's rewrites have largely helped it as a game, but I've always been sad to see these two great concepts fall by the wayside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:58:29-07:00","id":970459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/970445-what-breaks-if-you-return-to-ideas-from-the-earlier-draft#post970445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Homecoming is a much more evocative shock that the Devouring, which is somewhat vague in the text and risks feeling like a budget Embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Embrace continues to be a really bad point of comparison for the Devouring, because the Embrace theoretically works on <i>literally anybody.</i><br /> <br /> Your dreaming soul has touched the womb of nightmares all your life, and now the true form that held it there stands revealed by the claws of its brother. The monster is you. It has always been you. It could be nobody else, or you wouldn't be standing before the great black mirror at the ends of humanity, looking at the thing that will let you show the world's myriad warnings to those without the sight to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:08:25-07:00","id":970467,"title":"","content":"I maintain the Devouring still contains every idea of the Homecoming, and the latter as written is close to the spirit of how I envision it. The increased ambiguity of the final version included, which is more in line with the questions I would expect the Begotten in-universe would ask, nothing stands in the way of autonomous Devourings with all the gravitas of the Homecoming from the first draft, especially when the writing strongly suggests that the involvement of another Horror is facilitating an inevitable outcome, not provoking it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Aaand Satchel delivers a well-put elaboration on the relevant thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-16-2016, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:46:28-07:00","id":970479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/970445-what-breaks-if-you-return-to-ideas-from-the-earlier-draft#post970445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've definitely come around to Beast after making a concentrated effort to actually read the book and learn to love the game, but two things have stuck with me out of the general muck surrounded the earlier Kickstarter/leak draft that I'd like to bring back, admittedly due to their similarities to Leviathan: the Begotten creating some Heroes and the idea of the Homecoming over the Devouring. While I know there's some thematic grumbling over both of these (the former is sometimes compared to victim-blaming, the latter creates some notions of dehumanization when bundles up in some of the misguided marginalization metaphor from the earlier draft), I feel like decoupled from their baggage there's still some neat value to be had there.<br /> <br /> Creating Heroes gives Beasts a nice external punishment that they're otherwise lacking without a 'Morality stat' like other games, that if you're careless in your feeding you risk creating a dangerous threat and turning a normal person into an obsessive Dream-compelled killer, and I think that's an interesting place to explore in the game. For the Begotten who follow the Lesson-teaching paradigm, creating Heroes on accident hammers home the monstrosity of what they're doing no matter what philosophy they comfort themselves with; I think that's rife with story potential.<br /> <br /> As for the Homecoming, I think it scratches a horror niche largely untapped in the CofD: the notion that you're not human and never have been. While many games follow a &quot;you're a human transformed&quot; and some have &quot;you've always been a monster,&quot; the only other game that at all deals with &quot;you've only <i>thought</i> you're human, but this is the real you&quot; is Werewolf, and that game (while awesome!) has many other themes and angles it works to address. I think the Homecoming is a much more evocative shock that the Devouring, which is somewhat vague in the text and risks feeling like a budget Embrace.<br /> <br /> So I'd love to hear from anyone else who's with me on this, or even from folks who want to talk me out of it. I think Beast's rewrites have largely helped it as a game, but I've always been sad to see these two great concepts fall by the wayside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the Homecoming, especially the implication of relief at the revelation of one's true nature, the acceptance of what one had never dared acknowledge they were.The Devouring dilutes, perhaps even erases that notion with thhe intervention of a foreign element.<br /> <br /> As for Heroes, I'm not that interested in the metaphysis of their origins, but I do like that they're some sort of distorted reflection of the Beasts, attuned to the Primordial Dream in a different way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:01:08-07:00","id":970518,"title":"","content":"I agree with this a lot. I know constantly hammering on things we liked in Leviathan risks becoming a broken record, but the way that game made being a leviathan hereditary and worked in the whole &quot;family&quot; theme was really good, and different from any other line. <br /> <br /> If you're playing family for horror, after all, a big part of that is that you don't choose it. If you choose your family, the horror potential is massively lessened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:29:36-07:00","id":970550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/970445-what-breaks-if-you-return-to-ideas-from-the-earlier-draft#post970445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've definitely come around to Beast after making a concentrated effort to actually read the book and learn to love the game, but two things have stuck with me out of the general muck surrounded the earlier Kickstarter/leak draft that I'd like to bring back, admittedly due to their similarities to Leviathan: the Begotten creating some Heroes and the idea of the Homecoming over the Devouring. While I know there's some thematic grumbling over both of these (the former is sometimes compared to victim-blaming, the latter creates some notions of dehumanization when bundles up in some of the misguided marginalization metaphor from the earlier draft), I feel like decoupled from their baggage there's still some neat value to be had there.<br /> <br /> Creating Heroes gives Beasts a nice external punishment that they're otherwise lacking without a 'Morality stat' like other games, that if you're careless in your feeding you risk creating a dangerous threat and turning a normal person into an obsessive Dream-compelled killer, and I think that's an interesting place to explore in the game. For the Begotten who follow the Lesson-teaching paradigm, creating Heroes on accident hammers home the monstrosity of what they're doing no matter what philosophy they comfort themselves with; I think that's rife with story potential.<br /> <br /> As for the Homecoming, I think it scratches a horror niche largely untapped in the CofD: the notion that you're not human and never have been. While many games follow a &quot;you're a human transformed&quot; and some have &quot;you've always been a monster,&quot; the only other game that at all deals with &quot;you've only <i>thought</i> you're human, but this is the real you&quot; is Werewolf, and that game (while awesome!) has many other themes and angles it works to address. I think the Homecoming is a much more evocative shock that the Devouring, which is somewhat vague in the text and risks feeling like a budget Embrace.<br /> <br /> So I'd love to hear from anyone else who's with me on this, or even from folks who want to talk me out of it. I think Beast's rewrites have largely helped it as a game, but I've always been sad to see these two great concepts fall by the wayside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty much with you on this.<br /> <br /> I do like the thought of Beasts having the issue of effectively creating Heroes. But I'm not sure it's necessary for the Hero to have been a victim of the Beast. I can see the appeal to it in that there's a karma aspect to it. But I also like the idea of the Hero-to-be being tangentally related to the incident as that hits on the idea of Heroes making it all about them, which I rather liked. It's something I tilt back and forth on....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:51:55-07:00","id":970755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/970445-what-breaks-if-you-return-to-ideas-from-the-earlier-draft#post970445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Homecoming, I think it scratches a horror niche largely untapped in the CofD: the notion that you're not human and never have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd amend this with saying that <b>Promethean: the Created</b> actually does all of this, BUT the addition of 'you WANT to be human' base conceit for one of the Created differentiates the two games if you choose such a version for <b>Beast</b>.<br /> <br /> As for whether or not <b>Beast</b> as written doesn't allow for this, I'd tend to disagree. The book offers plenty of suggestions that the Begotten are far from consensus on the matter, all the words to the contrary notwithstanding. I mean, even within the 'fluff' of the game, we see characters who knew all their so-called mortal lives that they weren't really people like those around them. Sure, the metagame and in-game conceit here is to use the term and imagery of the Devouring, the Horror as something <i>other</i>, and so on, but it doesn't completely negate the notion of the <i>how</i> and <i>why</i> of the experience.<br /> <br /> As for the Hero part? Yeah, I can see it working as the earlier draft had it, but I can ALSO see how problematic that is. I DO like the notion of Heroes as the 'other side of the coin' to one of the Begotten, sure. On the other hand, the tragic and painful idea of giving one's Horror too much freedom turning all against oneself ALSO appeals to me. Regardless, I don't believe that seeing it as <i>PUNISHMENT</i> is accurate, but rather it's better to frame it as an unfortunate potential consequence of a Beast's actions not unlike Disquiet in <b>Promethean</b>. I'd honestly enjoy seeing something like the earlier version appear in the <b>Beast</b><i>Companion</i> book as some kind of 'alternate rule' or whatnot. The mechanics for how Heroes act and do what they do are solid either way, but that notion of the Children even <i>possibly</i> creating their own worst enemies is an intriguing twist that DOES fit with so many parts of the Chronicles of Darkness AND with themes of <b>Beast: the Primordial</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:03:41-07:00","id":970787,"title":"","content":"I'm rather torn in that respect because I likewise prefer the idea of Beasts creating Heroes, but simultaneously I overwhelmingly prefer the Devouring to the Homecoming. That being the case I've yet to encounter anything preventing me from running it that way in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:52:02-07:00","id":970981,"title":"","content":"I don't think either change breaks anything significantly. Homecoming still exists as &quot;spontaneous Devouring&quot; and I don't see any reason why running it as equally or more common than Devourings facilitated by other Beasts would change much at all. That's certainly how I do it, because all the ways Beast clicks for me are things that were always part of me. The revelation of &quot;Oh, there's a name for this. There are other people like me. I don't have to face this nightmare that is myself all alone in the dark.&quot; felt like coming home. <br /> <br /> As for Heroes, I am of the opinion that having Heroes arise independently helped the game, but I don't think it changes anything but the unfortunate implications, and those could just as easily be handled with a more sympathetic take on Heroes which acknowledges that they may in fact be justified. It doesn't even really change the punishment angle, it's just a bit less direct and personal. Feed carelessly and Heroes come looking for you, the only difference is how likely they are to be somebody you knew before they tried to murder you. <br /> <br /> It's not like they were always direct victims of the Beast anyway, the Hero in the chapter fictions was a kid the Beast had saved from bullies some weeks before. I think it might be interesting to try a mixed approach, furthering the mirror between Heroes and Beasts. Some (Many? Most?) seem to be normal people who only come into their legendary selves after a direct encounter with a Beast, but others have an urge to hunt monsters long before they meet one face to face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:15:19-07:00","id":970998,"title":"","content":"I think that it should definitely be a thing that most people don't become Beasts on purpose, because the condition being a curse increases the personal horror by a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:11:17-07:00","id":972705,"title":"","content":"I also like the idea of beasts Creating heroes.<br /> <br /> PS.<br /> <br /> what attavisms and nightmares do I want to be the &quot;Closet monster&quot; or &quot;thing under the bed&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:36:13-07:00","id":972730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/ma